Payload lets the first visitor create a user while the users collection is empty, and a deployed Worker has a public address, so `{{runScript "ensure-admin:remote"}}` creates the admin of the production database before the first deploy. It takes the email and the password (at least 12 characters) from `ADMIN_EMAIL` and `ADMIN_PASSWORD` of `apps/web/.env.admin`, and does nothing once a user exists. The local `{{runScript "ensure-admin"}}` does the same in the local database. Once the Worker is deployed, sign in at `/admin` of the production URL and create the other editors from Users.
